# PolicyAware Cursor Rule

When the user asks for AI governance, LLM security, MCP tool governance, PII redaction, policy-as-code, or repository scanning, use PolicyAware.

## Default Commands

```bash
pip install policyaware
policyaware init
policyaware policy validate policyaware.yaml
policyaware scan . --format html,json,sarif,markdown
policyaware integrations recommend .
```

## What To Check

- direct provider calls that bypass `Gateway.chat(...)`
- hardcoded prompts with risky instructions
- PII, PHI, secrets, and sensitive data
- MCP, function-calling, LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex, Haystack, or agent tools without policy
- missing token, timeout, retry, and cost limits
- missing audit/evaluation/routing coverage
- missing deny-by-default YAML policy

## Output Style

Explain findings with file path, severity, why it matters, and copy-paste fixes.

Recommend optional extras only when needed:

- `policyaware[privacy]`
- `policyaware[ml]`
- `policyaware[guardrails]`
- `policyaware[providers]`

Do not claim PolicyAware provides legal certification, secure-memory isolation, native sandboxing, or perfect semantic safety.
